     {"key": "frontline-mod3",
"title": "<b>Frontline</b>: ",
"data":{
   "shortURL": "https://frontline.frl",
   "creationTime": "1517865952.85",
   "title": "Frontline",
   "class": "GitGroup",
   "source": ""<h3>Introduction</h3>\n\n<p>Frontline is an Arma 3 PVP (player versus player) Modification, with tactical gameplay at its foundation. It&#39;s inspired by Squad, Project Reality and Tactical Battlefield and brings combined warfare to Arma 3. Instead of having a full realistic basis, we focus on providing balanced gameplay accessible for everyone.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>What differentiates our mod from the other PVP mods is the Dynamic Frontline feature that uses our own extension to execute Python code. The server generates a realistic frontline based on players&#39; locations which shifts the focus from a few key places on the map to the whole map at once. Players find themselves searching for the best strategy to achieve territorial dominance instead of always moving towards the zones usually pre-placed by the mission makers.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Since the group is&nbsp;international, it is a great way to improve your English. Indeed it has improved Lukasz&rsquo;s English skills&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>much more than working in his supposedly international company.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<h3>Volunteers Needed</h3>\n\n<p>&nbsp;They have a real problem finding people, because all of the volunteers spend all of their time playing the game.&nbsp; They currently have 5-6 core members, of which two are Python developers, one in Krakow. &nbsp; The others code in SQF, the Arma scripting language.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>They have lots of different tasks to work on:</p>\n\n<p>- The Dynamic Frontline regular python work for small changes (Python 3). &nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>-&nbsp;The Dynamic Frontline cython code for new improvements (Cython)</p>\n\n<p>- Some changes in our installer/launcher (Kivy Python2 code for desktop windows applications)</p>\n\n<p>- Administration/deployment scripts in python (Python 3)</p>\n\n<p>- Maybe some cloud related tasks (automatic starting up/shutting down servers) using the Scaleway API&nbsp;(Python 3)</p>\n\n<p>- Discord bots improvement (Python 3 asyncio code / django ORM)</p>\n\n<p>- Persistent scoring system (Python 3 django ORM probably - not started yet)</p>\n\n<p>- Additional website changes (Python 3, maybe just webmaster work)</p>\n\n<p>They also are looking for volunteers to do more than just Python. (map making, models making, Arma scripting, even PR people, in general).</p>\n\n<p>Of course all of the really easy tasks have been done, so what is available now is tasks for people with an intermediate level of Python knowledge (or higher) looking to either just help an unusual project or have something on their resume.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n"",
   "description": "Python Mods to the Arma 3 wargame, developers based in Krakow. ",
   "branchSize": "1"},
"a_attr": {"href": "https://frontline.frl"}},
